@* MobileEditGroup.razor — mobile version of the desktop EditGroup page.
   Route: /m/Admin/Groups/Edit/{GroupId:guid}
   Layout: MobileLayout

   PORTS a mobile-friendly subset of the desktop EditGroup.razor
   (1187 lines). The desktop page is a hybrid view + edit surface
   (summary card, edit form with Name + Salary Amount + locked
   Currency, Activate/Deactivate buttons, Bulk Apply Defaults card,
   help panel). MOBILE deliberately drops the desktop's heavy UX
   affordances (RadzenCard + EditForm + DataAnnotationsValidator +
   Radzen DialogService for DeactivateGroupDialog + JS.confirm for
   bulk apply + sticky help panel) — they belong on the desktop
   /Admin/Groups/Edit surface where there's room for two-column
   grids + modals + validators. What mobile keeps (mobile-friendly):

     - Page header with back button + group name + inline status
       badge (mirrors MobileUserDetail's .m-page-header-back pattern).
     - Summary card (read-only rows): Name, Salary (formatted +
       currency), Status badge, ActiveUserCount, CreatedAt,
       UpdatedAt (mirrors MobileSettings's .m-summary-card +
       .m-profile-row pattern).
     - Edit form (Manager + Admin only): Name input + Salary
       Amount input (with focus/blur format swap + Persian-digit
       swap) + locked-currency pill + Save button. Mirrors the
       desktop's two-command save flow (RenameCustomerGroupCommand
       if name changed + UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand if
       amount changed). Uses plain <input> + <button> elements
       (no EditForm + no DataAnnotationsValidator — mirrors
       MobileAdminCategories's inline-form pattern so no
       antiforgery token is needed and no form POST happens).
     - Activate/Deactivate card (Manager + Admin only):
         · Active group → Deactivate (destructive, opens an
           inline confirm panel with "Deactivate group
           '{name}'? ..." + Confirm/Cancel buttons, mirrors
           MobileUserDetail's _confirmingDeactivate pattern).
         · Inactive group → Activate (non-destructive, no
           confirmation — mirrors desktop's HandleActivateAsync).
       Per-action _busyAction string state machine (mirrors
       MobileAdminCategories's _busyKey + MobileUserDetail's
       _busyAction pattern).
     - Bulk Apply Defaults card (Manager + Admin only + group
       must be active) — closes the "reactivation gap" documented
       since Step 5: when a group is deactivated and new products
       are added during the inactive period, those new products
       have no limit row for the group. This card lets the admin
       bulk-fill missing limits with the default value (1) in one
       shot. The desktop uses JS.confirm() for the confirmation —
       mobile replaces it with an inline confirm panel (mirrors
       MobileUserDetail's _confirmingDeactivate pattern, per the
       task spec's "no JS interop beyond basic form interactions"
       rule).
     - Empty state (NotFoundTitle / NotFoundBody) when the handler
       returns Result.Failure (covers both genuinely-missing AND
       not-allowed-to-see — the desktop's GetCustomerGroupByIdQuery-
       Handler uses a "never leak existence" pattern, same as
       SaleDetail / ProductDetail / UserDetail).
     - Footer with Loc["Version"].

   NOT PORTED TO MOBILE (per task spec — these belong on desktop):
     - The desktop's sticky help panel (.help-panel with 5 bullet
       points about Rename / SalaryImmediate / SalaryNegative /
       CurrencyLocked / Deactivate). The hints are too dense for
       a mobile viewport; the desktop's SalaryHint one-liner
       under the amount field captures the most important warning
       (salary changes take effect immediately for new purchases;
       doesn't retroactively recalculate current month).
     - The desktop's EditForm + DataAnnotationsValidator +
       [Required]/[StringLength]/[Range] attributes. Mobile uses
       plain <input> + manual validation in HandleSaveAsync
       (check empty name → toast error; check parse-fail salary
       → toast error). Same simplification MobileAdminCategories
       uses for its inline add/rename forms.
     - The desktop's Radzen DialogService (DeactivateGroupDialog
       with 3-second countdown). Mobile replaces with a single
       inline-confirm panel (mirrors MobileCart's _confirmingClear
       pattern — same friction, lighter UX).
     - The desktop's JS.confirm() for bulk-apply. Mobile replaces
       with the SAME inline-confirm pattern (the task spec says
       "no JS interop beyond basic form interactions" — the
       desktop's window.confirm() popup is also jarring on a
       mobile viewport).
     - The desktop's _submitError inline banner. Mobile surfaces
       errors via Toast only (matches the gold-standard
       MobileProducts.razor + MobileUserDetail.razor pattern).
     - The desktop's _isBulkApplyingDefaults spinner on the bulk
       button + _isSubmitting shared flag. Mobile uses a separate
       _isBulkApplyingDefaults bool (no concurrent-action guard
       needed since bulk-apply is a one-shot dispatch that disables
       every other button on the page while in flight).

   NOT IN DESKTOP (and thus not on mobile either):
     The task spec mentioned "Members list — .m-list of group
     members, each row showing: full name, worker id, status badge.
     Optional remove-member button per row". The desktop EditGroup
     page does NOT have a members list — the only member-related
     info it shows is `ActiveUserCount` (a single integer in the
     summary card). The CustomerGroupDto does NOT expose a members
     collection (only `ActiveUserCount`), and the desktop page
     does NOT invoke AddUserToGroupCommand / RemoveUserFromGroup-
     Command (those commands live in TakOne.Application.Users.Commands,
     are invoked from the desktop UserDetail page, not from
     EditGroup). Per the task spec's "Do NOT invent new DTOs or
     queries — only use the existing ones the desktop page uses"
     rule, mobile mirrors the desktop verbatim — NO members list
     on the mobile EditGroup page either. The ActiveUserCount is
     shown in the summary card (same as desktop). Member management
     (assign user to group / remove user from group) is performed
     on the dedicated /m/Admin/Users surface (where the mobile
     UserDetail page can host those flows in a future round).

   BACKEND CONTRACT (mirrors desktop EditGroup.razor):
     - Load: GetCustomerGroupByIdQuery { GroupId } →
       Result<CustomerGroupDto>. [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager,
       Admin)] — Employee viewers are allowed in with a view-only
       scope (the edit form + activate/deactivate + bulk-apply
       cards are hidden via _isAdmin || _isManagerOnly). The
       handler returns Result.Failure with a generic "not found"
       for both genuinely-missing AND not-allowed-to-see viewers
       (defense-in-depth — never leaks that the group exists).
     - Rename: RenameCustomerGroupCommand(GroupId, NewName) →
       Result. [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)] — the mobile UI's
       _isAdmin || _isManagerOnly gate is a UX nicety, NOT a
       security boundary (backend rejects Employees + below).
     - Update Salary: UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand(GroupId,
       NewSalaryAmount) → Result. [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)].
       The salary's CURRENCY cannot be changed via this command —
       changing currency would invalidate already-purchased
       products priced in the old currency. To change currency,
       deactivate this group and create a new one (the form shows
       the currency as a locked pill to communicate this).
     - Activate: ActivateCustomerGroupCommand(GroupId) → Result.
       [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)] — idempotent (activating an
       already-active group is a no-op).
     - Deactivate: DeactivateCustomerGroupCommand(GroupId) →
       Result. [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)] — idempotent + soft-
       delete (IsActive = false; the row stays for audit).
     - Bulk Apply Defaults: BulkApplyDefaultsForGroupCommand(
       GroupId) → Result<BulkApplyDefaultsResult>. [RequireRoles(
       Manager, Admin)]. The handler rejects inactive groups —
       the UI hides the bulk-apply card when the group is inactive
       (mirrors desktop's @if (_group.IsActive) gate).

   ROLE-RESOLUTION PATTERN (matches desktop EditGroup.razor +
   MobileManageGroups.razor):
     _isAdmin, _isManagerOnly are computed in OnInitializedAsync
     via AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync() — NOT
     via ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false for
     everyone in interactive Blazor Server mode because
     HttpContext is null over the SignalR circuit). Same pattern
     as the desktop EditGroup.razor + MobileManageGroups.razor +
     MobileAdminUsers.razor. The Wolverine command handlers ALSO
     enforce [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)] server-side as
     defense-in-depth — the UI's _isAdmin || _isManagerOnly gate
     is a UX nicety, NOT a security boundary.

   MONEY: The salary amount is bound to a STRING field
   (_formSalaryAmount), NOT a decimal. Three reasons (mirrors
   the desktop's rationale verbatim):
     1. IRR amounts are whole Rial — never show 2 decimal digits.
     2. Need thousands separators (N0 format).
     3. Need Persian digits (۰-۹) when the UI culture is fa-IR.
   So: bind a string, format on blur (FormatSalaryForDisplay),
   parse on focus (raw invariant number for easy editing) and on
   submit (TryParseAmount). The onfocus/onblur swap is the only
   reliable way to get Persian digits out of .NET (NativeDigits
   is informational-only — see CultureFormat.cs header comment).

   ROUTE PARAMETER:
     `GroupId` is a Guid bound from the URL via [Parameter]. The
     @page constraint `{GroupId:guid}` validates the URL segment
     is parseable as a Guid before this component even loads —
     a malformed URL gets a 404 from the router, not a runtime
     exception here. The route param name is `GroupId` (matches
     the desktop EditGroup.razor's param name + the underlying
     GetCustomerGroupByIdQuery field name for symmetry).

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All buttons are regular <button>
     elements with async @onclick handlers that dispatch commands
     via Wolverine. The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery token is
     established at circuit start. No form POST happens. (Same
     as MobileAdminCategories + MobileUserDetail + MobileProductDetail.)

   NAVIGATION TARGETS:
     /m/Admin/Groups (Back button + NotFoundBody's "Back to
     groups" button — forceLoad:false so in-circuit navigation
     preserves the MobileLayout shell + BottomNav state, matches
     MobileUserDetail's GoToUsers pattern).
*@

@page "/m/Admin/Groups/Edit/{GroupId:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]
@layout TakOne.WebUI.Components.Layout.MobileLayout.MobileLayout

@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.ActivateCustomerGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.BulkApplyDefaultsForGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.DeactivateCustomerGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.RenameCustomerGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.UpdateCustomerGroupSalary
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Queries.GetCustomerGroupById
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services

@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<MobileEditGroup> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast

<PageTitle>@(_group is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{_group.Name} — {Loc["PageTitle"]}")</PageTitle>

@if (_isLoading)
{
    <div class="m-loading">
        <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
        <p>@Loc["Loading"]</p>
    </div>
}
else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
{
    <div class="m-error-box">
        <p>@_loadError</p>
        <button class="m-btn m-btn-secondary" @onclick="LoadAsync">@Loc["RetryButton"]</button>
    </div>
}
else if (_group is null)
{
    @* Not-found / not-allowed: the handler returns Result.Failure with a
       generic "Customer group '...' was not found." message for both
       genuinely-missing groups AND not-allowed-to-see viewers (defense-
       in-depth — never leaks that the group exists). Either way the user
       sees the same friendly NotFoundTitle / NotFoundBody message + a
       Back-to-groups button. Same pattern as MobileSaleDetail /
       MobileProductDetail / MobileUserDetail. *@
    <div class="m-empty">
        <p><strong>@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]</strong></p>
        <p>@Loc["NotFoundBody"]</p>
        <button class="m-btn m-btn-secondary" @onclick="GoToGroups">@Loc["BackToGroups"]</button>
    </div>
}
else
{
    @* ── 1. Page header — back button + group name + inline status
           badge. The .m-page-header-back wrapper + .m-back-btn +
           .m-page-header-text classes are mobile-detail-specific (also
           used by MobileSaleDetail + MobileProductDetail + MobileUserDetail)
           — the orchestrator adds them to mobile.css in a later pass
           (until then the page renders unstyled-but-functional). *@
    <div class="m-page-header-back">
        <button type="button"
                class="m-back-btn"
                aria-label="@Loc["BackToGroups"]"
                title="@Loc["BackToGroups"]"
                @onclick="GoToGroups">
            <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" style="width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem;">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
        <div class="m-page-header-text">
            <h1 class="m-page-title">@_group.Name</h1>
            <p class="m-page-subtitle">@Loc["PageSubtitle"]</p>
        </div>
        <span class="m-badge @(_group.IsActive ? "m-badge-success" : "m-badge-danger")">
            @(_group.IsActive ? Loc["StatusActive"] : Loc["StatusInactive"])
        </span>
    </div>

    @* ── 2. Summary card — read-only identity + audit fields. Mirrors
           MobileSettings.razor's .m-summary-card + .m-profile-row pattern
           + MobileUserDetail.razor's profile-card rendering. Laid out
           vertically for mobile (the desktop's 2-col .profile-grid is too
           dense for a 360px viewport). The ActiveUserCount row shows
           Loc["NoActiveUsers"] when the count is 0 so the row reads
           gracefully instead of "0" (mirrors the desktop's @if rule). *@
    <div class="m-summary-card">
        <div class="m-card-section-title">@Loc["SummaryCardTitle"]</div>

        <div class="m-profile-row">
            <span class="m-profile-label">@Loc["ColName"]</span>
            <span class="m-profile-value">@_group.Name</span>
        </div>

        <div class="m-profile-row">
            <span class="m-profile-label">@Loc["ColSalary"]</span>
            <span class="m-profile-value">
                @FormatSalaryAmount(_group.Salary.Amount)
                <span class="m-profile-muted" style="margin-inline-start: 0.25rem;">@_group.Salary.Currency</span>
            </span>
        </div>

        <div class="m-profile-row">
            <span class="m-profile-label">@Loc["ColStatus"]</span>
            <span class="m-profile-value">
                @if (_group.IsActive)
                {
                    <span class="m-badge m-badge-success">@Loc["StatusActive"]</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="m-badge m-badge-danger">@Loc["StatusInactive"]</span>
                }
            </span>
        </div>

        <div class="m-profile-row">
            <span class="m-profile-label">@Loc["ColActiveUsers"]</span>
            <span class="m-profile-value">
                @if (_group.ActiveUserCount == 0)
                {
                    <span class="m-profile-muted">@Loc["NoActiveUsers"]</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    @FormatInt(_group.ActiveUserCount)
                }
            </span>
        </div>

        <div class="m-profile-row">
            <span class="m-profile-label">@Loc["ColCreatedAt"]</span>
            <span class="m-profile-value">@FormatDate(_group.CreatedAtUtc)</span>
        </div>

        <div class="m-profile-row">
            <span class="m-profile-label">@Loc["ColUpdatedAt"]</span>
            <span class="m-profile-value">@FormatDate(_group.UpdatedAtUtc)</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ── 3. Edit form — Manager + Admin only. Employees see the summary
           card only (the edit form + activate/deactivate + bulk-apply
           cards are hidden). The form is gated BOTH client-side (this
           @if block) AND server-side (each command has [RequireRoles(
           Manager, Admin)]). Same role-scope rule as the desktop
           EditGroup.razor's @if (_isAdmin || _isManagerOnly) gate. *@
    @if (_isAdmin || _isManagerOnly)
    {
        <div class="m-summary-card">
            <div class="m-card-section-title">@Loc["EditFormCardTitle"]</div>

            @* ── Name input — bound to _formName, plain <input> with
                   @oninput (no @bind — mirrors MobileAdminCategories's
                   inline-add form pattern). Plain <input> avoids the
                   @bind-vs-@onblur conflict on the salary field below;
                   for consistency we use the same plain-input pattern
                   for the Name field too. *@
            <div class="m-form-field">
                <label class="m-form-label">@Loc["FieldName"]</label>
                <input class="m-input"
                       type="text"
                       value="@_formName"
                       placeholder="@Loc["FieldNamePlaceholder"]"
                       @oninput='@(e => _formName = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")'
                       @onkeypress='@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleSaveAsync(); })' />
            </div>

            @* ── Salary Amount input — bound to _formSalaryAmount (string
                   NOT decimal, see header comment for the rationale).
                   The @onfocus/@onblur swap shows the raw invariant
                   number while editing (easy typing) and the formatted
                   (thousand-separated + Persian-digit) value when not
                   editing. Mirrors the desktop's OnSalaryAmountFocus /
                   OnSalaryAmountBlur verbatim — the only reliable way to
                   get Persian digits out of .NET is the manual swap in
                   CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits (NativeDigits is
                   informational-only).

                   Currency is LOCKED — shown as a read-only pill next to
                   the amount field. Changing currency would invalidate
                   already-purchased products priced in the old currency
                   (the salary's currency is preserved on the aggregate
                   by UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand — it only accepts
                   the amount). To use a different currency, the admin
                   must deactivate this group and create a new one. *@
            <div class="m-form-field">
                <label class="m-form-label">@Loc["FieldSalary"]</label>

                <div class="m-salary-row">
                    <input class="m-input m-salary-amount"
                           type="text"
                           inputmode="decimal"
                           value="@_formSalaryAmount"
                           placeholder="@Loc["FieldAmountPlaceholder"]"
                           style="direction: ltr; text-align: left;"
                           @oninput='@(e => _formSalaryAmount = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")'
                           @onfocus="OnSalaryAmountFocus"
                           @onblur="OnSalaryAmountBlur" />

                    <span class="m-currency-pill"
                          title="@Loc["CurrencyLockedTitle"]">
                        <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" style="width: 0.875rem; height: 0.875rem;">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 15v2m-6 4h12a2 2 0 002-2v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2zm10-10V7a4 4 0 00-8 0v4h8z" />
                        </svg>
                        @_formSalaryCurrency
                    </span>
                </div>

                <p class="m-form-hint">@Loc["SalaryHint"]</p>
            </div>

            @* ── Save button — dispatches RenameCustomerGroupCommand (if
                   name changed) AND UpdateCustomerGroupSalaryCommand (if
                   amount changed). Both run in their own Wolverine
                   transaction; if either fails the other is NOT rolled
                   back (they're independent mutations on the same
                   aggregate; the user can fix the failing one and retry).
                   On success: Toast.Success + ReloadGroupSilentlyAsync
                   so the summary card's Salary/Name/UpdatedAt rows
                   refresh without a full-page reload. *@
            <button type="button"
                    class="m-btn m-btn-primary m-btn-block"
                    disabled="@_isBusy"
                    @onclick="HandleSaveAsync">
                @if (_isBusy)
                {
                    <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" style="width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem;">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                    </svg>
                }
                @Loc["SaveButton"]
            </button>
        </div>

        @* ── 4. Activate / Deactivate card — Manager + Admin only (the
               edit form @if already gates this section). Mirrors the
               desktop's form-actions row, but moved into its own card
               for the mobile vertical-stack layout.

               Per-action _busyAction string state machine (mirrors
               MobileAdminCategories's _busyKey + MobileUserDetail's
               _busyAction pattern): "action:activate" or
               "action:deactivate" — the finally block only clears the
               flag when it still matches this action's key (prevents a
               stale reset from a concurrent action). Disabled buttons
               render a small spinner to acknowledge the click. *@

        @* Active group → Deactivate (destructive, requires
               confirmation). Inline confirm flow mirrors MobileCart's
               _confirmingClear + MobileUserDetail's _confirmingDeactivate
               pattern: clicking the Deactivate button opens an inline
               panel with the confirm prompt + Confirm/Cancel buttons.
               No 3-second countdown like the desktop's DeactivateGroup-
               Dialog — mobile keeps the friction minimal but the confirm
               step prevents reflex clicks. *@
        <div class="m-summary-card">
            <div class="m-card-section-title">@Loc["ActionsCardTitle"]</div>

            @if (_group.IsActive)
            {
                @if (_confirmingDeactivate)
                {
                    <div class="m-inline-confirm">
                        <p class="m-inline-confirm-text">
                            @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ConfirmDeactivate"], _group.Name)
                        </p>
                        <div class="m-inline-confirm-actions">
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="m-btn m-btn-secondary m-btn-sm"
                                    disabled="@(_busyAction == "action:deactivate")"
                                    @onclick="CancelDeactivate">
                                @Loc["CancelButton"]
                            </button>
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="m-btn m-btn-danger m-btn-sm"
                                    disabled="@(_busyAction is not null)"
                                    @onclick="HandleDeactivateAsync">
                                @if (_busyAction == "action:deactivate")
                                {
                                    <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small" />
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" style="width: 1rem; height: 1rem;">
                                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5" />
                                    </svg>
                                }
                                @Loc["DeactivateButton"]
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <button type="button"
                            class="m-btn m-btn-danger m-btn-block"
                            disabled="@(_busyAction is not null)"
                            @onclick="StartDeactivateConfirm">
                        @if (_busyAction == "action:deactivate")
                        {
                            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" style="width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem;">
                                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M18.364 18.364A9 9 0 005.636 5.636m12.728 12.728A9 9 0 015.636 18.364m12.728-12.728L5.636 18.364" />
                            </svg>
                        }
                        @Loc["DeactivateButton"]
                    </button>
                }
            }
            else
            {
                @* Inactive group → Activate (non-destructive, no
                       confirmation — mirrors the desktop's
                       HandleActivateAsync). Activation is a restore from
                       soft-delete, so the friction isn't needed. *@
                <button type="button"
                        class="m-btn m-btn-primary m-btn-block"
                        disabled="@(_busyAction is not null)"
                        @onclick="HandleActivateAsync">
                    @if (_busyAction == "action:activate")
                    {
                        <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" style="width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem;">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5" />
                        </svg>
                    }
                    @Loc["ActivateButton"]
                </button>
            }
        </div>

        @* ── 5. Bulk Apply Defaults card — Manager + Admin only + group
               must be active. Closes the "reactivation gap" documented
               since Step 5: when a group is deactivated and new products
               are added during the inactive period, those new products
               have NO limit row for the group (CreateProduct's Phase-1
               auto-default loop only iterates ACTIVE groups, by design).
               This card lets the admin bulk-fill missing limits with the
               default value (1) in one shot. The desktop uses
               JS.confirm() for confirmation — mobile replaces with an
               inline-confirm panel (mirrors MobileUserDetail's
               _confirmingDeactivate pattern, per the task spec's "no JS
               interop beyond basic form interactions" rule).

               The card is visually distinct (warning tone + auto_fix_high
               icon) to signal that this is a bulk operation across the
               entire catalog, not a single-row mutation. The card is
               hidden when the group is inactive (the handler also rejects
               inactive groups with a friendly error — the UI hides the
               card preemptively to avoid a dead-end click). *@
        @if (_group.IsActive)
        {
            <div class="m-summary-card m-bulk-card">
                <div class="m-card-section-title">@Loc["BulkDefaultsCardTitle"]</div>

                <p class="m-card-text">@Loc["BulkDefaultsDescription"]</p>

                @if (_confirmingBulkApply)
                {
                    <div class="m-inline-confirm">
                        <p class="m-inline-confirm-text">
                            @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ConfirmBulkApplyDefaults"], _group.Name)
                        </p>
                        <div class="m-inline-confirm-actions">
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="m-btn m-btn-secondary m-btn-sm"
                                    disabled="@_isBulkApplyingDefaults"
                                    @onclick="CancelBulkApply">
                                @Loc["CancelButton"]
                            </button>
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="m-btn m-btn-primary m-btn-sm"
                                    disabled="@_isBulkApplyingDefaults"
                                    @onclick="HandleBulkApplyDefaultsAsync">
                                @if (_isBulkApplyingDefaults)
                                {
                                    <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small" />
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" style="width: 1rem; height: 1rem;">
                                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5" />
                                    </svg>
                                }
                                @Loc["BulkApplyDefaultsButton"]
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <button type="button"
                            class="m-btn m-btn-secondary m-btn-block"
                            disabled="@_isBulkApplyingDefaults"
                            @onclick="StartBulkApplyConfirm">
                        @if (_isBulkApplyingDefaults)
                        {
                            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" style="width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem;">
                                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.42 15.17L17.25 21A2.652 2.652 0 0021 17.25l-5.871-5.871M11.42 15.17l-2.496 3.394a1 1 0 01-1.515.119L3 14.5 5.5 12m5.921 3.17l5.871-5.871M14.5 5.5L17 3l4 4-2.5 2.5m-9.5 2.5L4 17.5 6.5 20l4.5-4.5"
                                />
                            </svg>
                        }
                        @Loc["BulkApplyDefaultsButton"]
                    </button>
                }
            </div>
        }
    }

    @* ── 6. Footer — version string. Same .m-footer pattern as the other
           mobile pages. *@
    <div class="m-footer">
        @Loc["Version"]
    </div>
}

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Group ID from the route (/m/Admin/Groups/Edit/{GroupId:guid}).
    /// Bound by the Blazor router — a malformed Guid segment triggers
    /// the router's 404 template before this component loads. The route
    /// param name is `GroupId` (matches the desktop EditGroup.razor's
    /// param name + the underlying GetCustomerGroupByIdQuery field
    /// name for symmetry).
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid GroupId { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The loaded CustomerGroupDto (Id, Name, Salary (MoneyDto),
    /// IsActive, CreatedAtUtc, UpdatedAtUtc, ActiveUserCount). Null
    /// when the load failed OR when the handler returned Result.Failure
    /// (covers both genuinely-missing AND viewer-not-allowed — the
    /// markup's not-found branch handles both cases with the same
    /// friendly message).
    /// </summary>
    private CustomerGroupDto? _group;

    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    // ── Form state (mirrors desktop EditGroup.razor's _model fields) ──

    /// <summary>
    /// Form field: group name (bound to the Name input via @oninput).
    /// Pre-filled from _group.Name in LoadAsync. Trimmed in HandleSaveAsync
    /// before comparison + dispatch.
    /// </summary>
